Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:49:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PETSc copy and BoomerAMG elasticity: remarks of the review

- the Elasticity strategy of BoomerAMG requires unknowns with as many
  components as the dimension of the mesh, which shall be the space
  dimension: MFEM computes the rigid body modes with the dimension of the
  mesh (a surface mesh in a 3D space with 3 components still aborted);
  the test checks the error message of the refusal;
- the matrices of hypre are copied on their own communicator, without
  the communication of the entries of other processes at the assembly
  (MAT_NO_OFF_PROC_ENTRIES);
- PETScSolversTest compares the products by a vector of the matrix given
  to the Krylov solver of PETSc and of the matrix of hypre, for the
  Laplace equation and the linear elasticity;
- wording of the documentation: the tangent operator given to SNES is
  copied in the AIJ format of the host, on the host as on a GPU.
